Feature: Routing

  Background:
    Given I Visit "/"
    And I Add "buy some cheese"
    And I Add "feed the cat"
    And I Add "book a doctors appointment"
    And I Tick the Todo "feed the cat"

  @fixme
  Scenario: Showing active todos
    When I Click the Link "Active"
    Then I should See "buy some cheese"
    And I should See "book a doctors appointment"
    But I should Not See "feed the cat"

  @fixme
  Scenario: Showing completed todos
    When I Click the Link "Completed"
    Then I should See "feed the cat"
    But I should Not See "buy some cheese"

  @fixme
  Scenario: Showing all todos
    When I Click the Link "Active"
    And I Click the Link "Completed"
    And I Click the Link "All"
    Then I should See "buy some cheese"
    And I should See "feed the cat"

  @fixme
  Scenario: The back button
    When I Click the Link "All"
    And I Click the Link "Active"
    And I Click the Link "Completed"
    Then I should Not See "buy some cheese"
    When I go Back
    Then I should See "buy some cheese"
    But I should Not See "feed the cat"
    When I go Back
    Then I should See "feed the cat"

  @fixme
  Scenario: The current filter is highlighted
    When I Click the Link "Active"
    Then I should be At "/#/active"
    When I Click the Link "Completed"
    Then I should be At "/#/completed"
